  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n10+3x-{x}^{2}\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=10+3x-{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/b85abe0f3c20d50c856d7f73a1b0afc82c637e8afc258d2c689801a44e5ea4a5.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-2\\le x\\le 5.$",
